# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML website following the latest official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:
- **source/index.html** - Added Vercel Web Analytics scripts to the `<head>` section

## Implementation Details

### Framework Detection:
This is a vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript static website with no framework dependencies. The project structure includes:
- index.html (main entry point)
- styles.css (styling)
- script.js (JavaScript functionality)
- Static assets (images, CV, etc.)

### Analytics Integration:
Following the official Vercel Analytics documentation for vanilla/static sites, I added two script tags to the HTML `<head>` section just before the closing `</head>` tag:

1. **Initialization script**: Sets up the `window.va` function to queue analytics calls
2. **Analytics loader**: Deferred loading of the Vercel insights script from `/_vercel/insights/script.js`

The implementation follows the exact pattern recommended in the Vercel documentation:
```html
<script>
    window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };
</script>
<script defer src="/_vercel/insights/script.js"></script>
```

## Why This Approach:
- **No package installation required**: Static HTML sites don't need the `@vercel/analytics` npm package
- **Automatic tracking**: Vercel automatically serves the analytics script at `/_vercel/insights/script.js` when deployed
- **Minimal overhead**: The script is loaded with the `defer` attribute to avoid blocking page rendering
- **Future-proof**: Uses the latest implementation pattern from Vercel's official documentation

## Next Steps:
Once deployed to Vercel, the analytics will automatically start tracking:
1. Page views
2. User sessions
3. Custom events (if implemented later)

To view analytics data:
1. Deploy the site to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Analytics data will appear in the dashboard after users visit the site

## Testing:
- Verified the HTML file loads correctly with a local HTTP server
- Confirmed the scripts are properly placed in the `<head>` section
- No build process or dependencies required for this static site

## Notes:
- No package.json exists, so no dependencies to install
- No build process required
- The analytics script will only load when deployed on Vercel
- For local development, the script will gracefully fail but won't break the site
